@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "customer.portal"

Feature: Project Details
	Testing the Project Details portlet.

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails
	* I generate a provisioning project name
	* I generate a provisioning company name
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | pjd.customer1                       |
	| Email Address | pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PJD                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer1                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | pjd.customer2                       |
	| Email Address | pjd.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PJD                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer2                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | pjd.partner1                      |
	| Email Address | pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PJD                               |
	| Last Name     | Partner1                          |
	* I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Name   | Zenpar - ${staticCompanyName} | |
	| Code   | ZENPARZENPAR                  | |
	| Status | Active                        | |
	* I assign the contact with the email address "pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" on the account "Zenpar - ${staticCompanyName}" to the following roles
	| Partner Manager |
	* I set the project details non abbreviated date method to true
	* I generate static start and end dates
	* I generate static full non abbreviated start and end dates
	* I generate future static full non abbreviated start and end dates
	* I generate past static full non abbreviated start and end dates
	* I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Zenpar - ${staticCompanyName}" and the product "Service Partnership" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	* I create an assigned team nested field for a team with the name "Zenpar - ${staticCompanyName}" assigned to the account "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	* I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Assigned Team Nested Field | ${staticAssignedTeamNestedField} | |
	| Code                       | PJDZENPJDZEN                     | |
	| Name                       | Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}    | |
	| Region                     | United States                    | |
	| Status                     | Active                           | |
	| Tier                       | T1                               | |
	* I assign the team with the name "Zenpar - ${staticCompanyName}" on the account "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Partner |
	* I assign the team with the name "Zenpar - ${staticCompanyName}" on the account "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| First Line Support |
	* I assign the contact with the email address "pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Requester |
	* I assign the contact with the email address "pjd.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support User  |
	* I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	* I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	* I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Portal Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	* I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Gold Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	* I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Commerce Subscription Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	* I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Commerce Connectors Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	* I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Enterprise Search - Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Gold Subscription"
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Partner"
	* I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Partner"
	* I wait for "1" minutes
	* the support organization with the code "PJDZENPJDZEN" should be part of the support site

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the first default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Zenpar - ${staticCompanyName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the second default user ID variable
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Zenpar - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| ZENPARZENPAR |
	| PJDZENPJDZEN |
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Gold Subscription"
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Limited Subscription"
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes via groovy
	| ZENPARZENPAR |
	| PJDZENPJDZEN |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pjd.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pjd.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pjd.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I tear down the product consumptions on koroneiki made by the account "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products
	| DXP Production                   |
	| Commerce Subscription Production |
	| Portal Production                |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pjd.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pjd.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Zenpar - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId2}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View project
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	@ help.center.smoke = "true"
	New projects created in PJD should be visible in the project details page.

	Given I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the Project Details page
	And I search for the project with the name "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I go to the project with the name "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	Then the project details with the following values should be visible
	| Project Code    | PJDZENPJDZEN                  |
	| State           | ACTIVE                        |
	| Level           | Platinum Subscription         |
	| Support Region  | United States                 |
	| Partner         | Zenpar - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| Partner Support | Zenpar - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| Tier            | T1                            |
	When I go to the Team Members tab
	Then the team member with the name "PJD Customer1" should be visible with the following values
	| Name  | PJD Customer1                       |
	| Role  | Support Requester                   |
	| Email | pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And the team member with the name "PJD Customer2" should be visible with the following values
	| Name  | PJD Customer2                       |
	| Role  | Support User                        |
	| Email | pjd.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	When I go to the Offerings tab
	Then the offering with the product name "Platinum Subscription" should be visible with the following values
	| Product          | Platinum Subscription                      |
	| Start Date       | ${staticFullNonAbbreviatedStartDate}       |
	| Support End Date | ${staticFullNonAbbreviatedOriginalEndDate} |
	| Instance Size    | 1                                          |
	| Quantity         | 1                                          |
	| Provisioned      | 0                                          |
	| State            | ACTIVE                                     |
	And the offering with the product name "DXP Production" should be visible with the following values
	| Product          | DXP Production  		                    |
	| Start Date       | ${staticFullNonAbbreviatedStartDate}       |
	| Support End Date | ${staticFullNonAbbreviatedOriginalEndDate} |
	| Instance Size    | 1               		                    |
	| Quantity         | 1               		                    |
	| Provisioned      | 0               		                    |
	| State            | ACTIVE          		                    |
	And the offering with the product name "Portal Production" should be visible with the following values
	| Product          | Portal Production                          |
	| Start Date       | ${staticFullNonAbbreviatedStartDate}       |
	| Support End Date | ${staticFullNonAbbreviatedOriginalEndDate} |
	| Instance Size    | 1                                          |
	| Quantity         | 1                                          |
	| Provisioned      | 0                                          |
	| State            | ACTIVE                                     |
	And the offering with the product name "Gold Subscription" should be visible with the following values
	| Product          | Gold Subscription                          |
	| Start Date       | ${staticFullNonAbbreviatedStartDate}       |
	| Support End Date | ${staticFullNonAbbreviatedOriginalEndDate} |
	| Instance Size    | 1                                          |
	| Quantity         | 1                                          |
	| Provisioned      | 0                                          |
	| State            | ACTIVE                                     |
	And the offering with the product name "Commerce Subscription Production" should be visible with the following values
	| Product          | Commerce Subscription Production           |
	| Start Date       | ${staticFullNonAbbreviatedStartDate}       |
	| Support End Date | ${staticFullNonAbbreviatedOriginalEndDate} |
	| Instance Size    | 1                                          |
	| Quantity         | 1                                          |
	| Provisioned      | 0                                          |
	| State            | ACTIVE                                     |
	And the offering with the product name "Enterprise Search - Production" should be visible with the following values
	| Product          | Enterprise Search - Production             |
	| Start Date       | ${staticFullNonAbbreviatedStartDate}       |
	| Support End Date | ${staticFullNonAbbreviatedOriginalEndDate} |
	| Instance Size    | 1                                          |
	| Quantity         | 1                                          |
	| Provisioned      | 0                                          |
	| State            | ACTIVE                                     |

Scenario: View past project
	New past projects created in PJD should be visible in the project details page.

	Given I generate past static start and end dates
	And I update a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "DXP Production" to have the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticPastEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticPastOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticPastStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                     | |
	And I update a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Platinum Subscription" to have the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticPastEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticPastOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticPastStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                     | |
	Given I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the Project Details page
	And I search for the project with the name "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I go to the project with the name "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	Then the project details with the following values should be visible
	| Project Code    | PJDZENPJDZEN                  |
	| State           | ACTIVE                        |
	| Level           | Gold Subscription             |
	| Support Region  | United States                 |
	| Partner         | Zenpar - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| Partner Support | Zenpar - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| Tier            | T1                            |
	When I go to the Team Members tab
	Then the team member with the name "PJD Customer1" should be visible with the following values
	| Name  | PJD Customer1                       |
	| Role  | Support Requester                   |
	| Email | pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And the team member with the name "PJD Customer2" should be visible with the following values
	| Name  | PJD Customer2                       |
	| Role  | Support User                        |
	| Email | pjd.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	When I go to the Offerings tab
	Then the offering with the product name "Platinum Subscription" should be visible with the following values
	| Product          | Platinum Subscription |
	| Instance Size    | -                     |
	| Quantity         | 0                     |
	| State            | EXPIRED               |
	And the offering with the product name "DXP Production" should be visible with the following values
	| Product          | DXP Production  |
	| Instance Size    | -               |
	| Quantity         | 0               |
	| State            | EXPIRED         |

