Scenario: View project offerings via Japanese localization
	Proper offering SLA values should be visible in the Japanese localized project details page.

	Given I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	Given I go to the "ja" localized Project Details page
	And I search for the project with the name "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I go to the project with the name "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I go to the localized Offerings tab
	Then the offering with the product name "Standard Subscription" should be visible with the following values
	| Product          | Standard Subscription |
	| Quantity         | 1                     |
	| State            | 有効                   |
	And the offering with the product name "Light Subscription" should be visible with the following values
	| Product          | Light Subscription |
	| Quantity         | 1                  |
	| State            | 有効                |

Scenario: Add portal environment details
	Users should be able to add portal environment details via the Project Details page.

	Given I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the Project Details page
	And I search for the project with the name "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I go to the project with the name "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I add an environment configuration with the following values
	| Name               | Zen Portal Environment One |
	| Product            | Portal Production          |
	| Liferay Version    | 6.2 EE                     |
	| Operating System   | Windows Server 2012        |
	| Java Version       | Oracle JDK 7               |
	| Application Server | Tomcat 7.0                 |
	| Database           | MariaDB 10.0               |
	| Cloud Services     | Azure SQL Databases        |
	| Browser            | Chrome                     |
	| Portal EXT         | portal-ext.properties      |
	| Patch Info         | patchinfo.txt              |
	Then the environment configuration with the name "Zen Portal Environment One" should be visible with the following values
	| Name               | Zen Portal Environment One |
	| Product            | Portal Production          |
	| Liferay Version    | 6.2 EE                     |
	| Operating System   | Windows Server 2012        |
	| Java Version       | Oracle JDK 7               |
	| Application Server | Tomcat 7.0                 |
	| Database           | MariaDB 10.0               |
	| Cloud Services     | Azure SQL Databases        |
	| Browser            | Chrome                     |
	| Portal EXT         | portal-ext.properties      |
	| Patch Info         | patchinfo.txt              |

Scenario: Add dxp environment details
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	Users should be able to add dxp environment details via the Project Details page.

	Given I delete a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Enterprise Search - Production"
	And I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the Project Details page
	And I search for the project with the name "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I go to the project with the name "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I add an environment configuration with the following values
	| Name               | Zen Portal Environment One |
	| Product            | DXP Production             |
	| Liferay Version    | 7.2	                      |
	| Operating System   | Windows Server 2019        |
	| Java Version       | Oracle JDK 11              |
	| Application Server | Tomcat 9.0                 |
	| Database           | MariaDB 10.2               |
	| Cloud Services     | Azure SQL Databases        |
	| Browser            | Chrome                     |
	| Search             | Solr 7.x                   |
	| Portal EXT         | portal-ext.properties      |
	| Patch Info         | patchinfo.txt              |
	Then the environment configuration with the name "Zen Portal Environment One" should be visible with the following values
	| Name               | Zen Portal Environment One |
	| Product            | DXP Production             |
	| Liferay Version    | 7.2	                      |
	| Operating System   | Windows Server 2019        |
	| Java Version       | Oracle JDK 11              |
	| Application Server | Tomcat 9.0                 |
	| Database           | MariaDB 10.2               |
	| Cloud Services     | Azure SQL Databases        |
	| Browser            | Chrome                     |
	| Search             | Solr 7.x                   |
	| Portal EXT         | portal-ext.properties      |
	| Patch Info         | patchinfo.txt              |

Scenario: Add dxp environment details on past subscription
	Users should be able to add dxp environment details on a past subscription via the Project Details page.

	Given I delete a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Enterprise Search - Production"
	And I delete a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Commerce Connectors Production"
	And I delete a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Commerce Subscription Production"
	And I delete a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Gold Subscription"
	And I delete a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Portal Production"
	And I generate past static start and end dates
	And I update a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "DXP Production" to have the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticPastEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticPastOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticPastStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                     | |
	And I update a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Platinum Subscription" to have the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticPastEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticPastOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticPastStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                     | |
	And I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the Project Details page
	And I search for the project with the name "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I go to the project with the name "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I add an environment configuration with the following values
	| Name               | Zen Portal Environment One |
