Scenario: View support instructions
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	Users should be able to view support instructions via the Project Details page.

	Given I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticKoroneikiAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticKoroneikiAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Pjdzen"
	And I click on the account with the name "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "Support" tab
	And I edit the following account fields and types to the following values under the account details tab
	| Support Instructions | Textarea | Support Instructions Content | |
	And I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the Project Details page
	And I search for the project with the name "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I go to the project with the name "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	Then the support instructions with the content "Support Instructions Content" should be visible

Scenario: View project offerings as customer and partner
	Projects created in PJD should have certain elements visible to customers and partners in the project details page.

	Given I generate past static start and end dates
	And I update a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Portal Production" to have the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticPastEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticPastOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticPastStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                     | |
	And I update a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Gold Subscription" to have the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticPastEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticPastOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticPastStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                     | |
	Then the support user with the email address "pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	And the support user with the email address "pjd.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	And the support user with the email address "pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	When I update the support password for user with the email address "pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I update the support password for user with the email address "pjd.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I update the support password for user with the email address "pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" to "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "pjd.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I log into the support homepage as "pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I go to the Project Details page
	And I go to the Offerings tab
	Then the offering with the product name "Portal Production" should not be visible
	And the offering with the product name "DXP Production" should be visible with the following values
	| Product          | DXP Production                             |
	| Start Date       | ${staticFullNonAbbreviatedStartDate}       |
	| Support End Date | ${staticFullNonAbbreviatedOriginalEndDate} |
	| Instance Size    | 1                                          |
	| Quantity         | 1                                          |
	And the offering with the product name "Commerce Subscription Production" should be visible with the following values
	| Product          | Commerce Subscription Production           |
	| Start Date       | ${staticFullNonAbbreviatedStartDate}       |
	| Support End Date | ${staticFullNonAbbreviatedOriginalEndDate} |
	| Instance Size    | 1                                          |
	| Quantity         | 1                                          |
	When I log out and log into the support homepage as "pjd.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I go to the Project Details page
	And I go to the Offerings tab
	Then the offering with the product name "Portal Production" should not be visible
	And the offering with the product name "DXP Production" should be visible with the following values
	| Product          | DXP Production                             |
	| Start Date       | ${staticFullNonAbbreviatedStartDate}       |
	| Support End Date | ${staticFullNonAbbreviatedOriginalEndDate} |
	| Instance Size    | 1                                          |
	| Quantity         | 1                                          |
	And the offering with the product name "Commerce Subscription Production" should be visible with the following values
	| Product          | Commerce Subscription Production           |
	| Start Date       | ${staticFullNonAbbreviatedStartDate}       |
	| Support End Date | ${staticFullNonAbbreviatedOriginalEndDate} |
	| Instance Size    | 1                                          |
	| Quantity         | 1                                          |
	When I log out and log into the support homepage as "pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" with password "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I go to the Project Details page
	And I go to the project with the name "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I go to the Offerings tab
	Then the offering with the product name "Portal Production" should be visible with the following values
	| Product          | Portal Production                              |
	| Start Date       | ${staticFullNonAbbreviatedPastStartDate}       |
	| Support End Date | ${staticFullNonAbbreviatedPastOriginalEndDate} |
	| Instance Size    | -                                              |
	| Quantity         | 0                                              |
	And the offering with the product name "DXP Production" should be visible with the following values
	| Product          | DXP Production                             |
	| Start Date       | ${staticFullNonAbbreviatedStartDate}       |
	| Support End Date | ${staticFullNonAbbreviatedOriginalEndDate} |
	| Instance Size    | 1                                          |
	| Quantity         | 1                                          |
	And the offering with the product name "Commerce Subscription Production" should be visible with the following values
	| Product          | Commerce Subscription Production           |
	| Start Date       | ${staticFullNonAbbreviatedStartDate}       |
	| Support End Date | ${staticFullNonAbbreviatedOriginalEndDate} |
