Scenario: View project details as non support requester or non support user
	Projects created in PJD should not be visible to a non support requester or non support user.

	Given I assign the contact with the email address "pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Member |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "pjd.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Member |
	And I remove the contact with the email address "pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" from the following roles
	| Support Requester |
	And I remove the contact with the email address "pjd.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" from the following roles
	| Support User  |
	Then the support user with the email address "pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	And the support user with the email address "pjd.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	When I update the support password for user with the email address "pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I update the support password for user with the email address "pjd.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "pjd.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I log into the support homepage as "pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I go to the Project Details page
	Then I should be able to view a no permission error message
	When I log out and log into the support homepage as "pjd.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I go to the Project Details page
	Then I should be able to view a no permission error message

