Scenario: View partner user access to the Self Provisioning portlet
	Partner users should be able to access the Self Provisioning portlet.

	Given I delete a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Enterprise Search - Production"
	And I delete a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Commerce Connectors Production"
	And I delete a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Commerce Subscription Production"
	And I delete a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Gold Subscription"
	And I delete a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Portal Production"
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the support organization with the code "ZENPARZENPAR" should be part of the support site
	And the support user with the email address "pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	When I update the support password for user with the email address "pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" to "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I log out and log into the support homepage as "pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" with password "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I go to the Self Provisioning page
	Then I should be able to view the following options in the Self Provisioning portlet
	| Project | Zenpar - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| Product | Commerce Subscription         |
	| Product | DXP                           |
	| Product | Portal                        |